message: "If you use this research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "R&D Alpha: Empirical Evidence on R&D Investment Intensity and Long-Term Stock Returns"
authors:
  - family-names: "Sehgal"
    given-names: "Abhishek"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/vastdreams/rd-alpha-research"
url: "https://research.finsoeasy.com"
abstract: >-
  Empirical research investigating the relationship between 
  R&D investment intensity and long-term stock returns. Finds a 
  statistically significant Q5-Q1 annual premium of +7.6%/yr 
  (Newey-West t = 2.78, win rate 71%) within the S&P 500 universe
  over 2010-2024.
keywords:
  - R&D intensity
  - stock returns
  - factor investing
  - quantitative finance
  - innovation premium
  - long-horizon returns
